+# Finite original-source A/B diagnostics
 
-The original export diagnostic001 stopped honestly at `ExportSpecctraDSN` returning false; observer JSON and DRC were not reached, and original inputs remained unchanged. The default `export` behavior is retained. An explicit `--observation context-only` now uses the unchanged production `floor_context.py final` observer, without DSN export or adapter work, then the same separate original-rule DRC. Actual context-only002 at `dbea85e796a1024ade7346568369283719289d86` completed both nonsaving stages with0opens/0blocking/7warnings/0exclusions; all original bytes and copied source-file bytes remain unchanged, with only a disposable DRC `.kicad_prl` added. The independent197-check audit passes. The source already contained its routes, and no autorouting or format/dependency qualification follows. All 52 pure controls pass; fabricated observations and process records do not establish native geometry, settings, routing, or compatibility.
+The existing controller now has two fixed `SourceSpec` profiles: default `lipo` and opt-in `paw3395`. There is no source-path or manifest-path CLI. Both use the same nonsaving observation and original-rule DRC lifecycle, unchanged 30-second wall/full waited-child CPU budget, 20 MiB output ceiling, isolated complete copies and network-denied native argv. The helper, tests, this README and `source_profiles.py` must all match the committed checkpoint and retained source snapshot. Legacy LiPo selectors and default worker argv remain unchanged.
+
+PAW3395 is pinned to the original 14-file / 2,163,350-byte acquisition at `.data/expansion005/paw3395`, receipt SHA `370f1c09157a7090fb725018bd7fa3ebb3d184d9163c1ee807110c674f2ac629`, board SHA `c2e8cebd0da804eb3912c6559ad6b3e725c1b29f744d616e1ebb22f1229f7740` and project SHA `4a0b352b482dd49a22aeea5599c44444e2d1dfad2ac77880c63152002445cdad`. Its original format is `20240108`, references are `property "Reference"`, and pad/route identities use `uuid`. The expected census is 18 footprints, 56 pads, 16 nonempty nets, 220 routes and one original zone. Its complete acquisition receipt, Git blobs, source sizes and hashes are checked; both stages retain complete original copies (4,326,700 bytes before generated output).
+
+The PAW diagnostic requires exactly the existing production rejection `unsupported: unknown rule severity semantics: zone_has_empty_net; unqualified board format version`. Neither reason is waived for routing. Original `zone_has_empty_net=error` stays unchanged; the pinned current KiCad registry does not establish enforcement of that legacy setting. Unchanged JSON or a clean report would not qualify it. The native result retains every reported finding and ignored key; `all_original_severity_enforcement_qualified`, format support, dependency closure and routing acceptance remain false. Optional external footprint/model resolution is not silently substituted. Native loading, export and DRC for this new profile have not yet run.
+
+After review and a verified source checkpoint, ROOT can execute once on its sole native lane:
+
+```sh
+python3 -B -m unittest discover -s experiments/lipo_native_diagnostic_v1 -p test_driver.py -v
+python3 -B experiments/lipo_native_diagnostic_v1/driver.py --source-profile paw3395 --observation export --output .runs/paw3395-native-diagnostic-001 --run-native
+```
+
+The shared revision has 59 focused pure controls, including the actual PAW source pins/census and two-stage mocked positive, cross-profile/identity/argv rejection and a completed-export/mapping-failure case. These fake native records do not qualify native behavior. A real-file publication regression first demonstrated that mutation or budget expiry during the final output scan could leave a positive summary. The corrected order scans output, repeats material checks, compares canonical and in-memory records, then checks caps. Invalidated positive/partial bytes are retained; corrective records reset qualification flags. Successful frozen export evidence is recorded before correspondence interpretation, so a later mismatch remains a failed observation with its first cause and actual DSN digest, not an invented export failure. These finite consistency samples are not atomic protection against a hostile concurrent writer.
